{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1450476-arcane-laws-of-the-fae","id":1450476,"title":"Arcane laws of the Fae?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-31T12:02:43-07:00","id":1450476,"title":"Arcane laws of the Fae?","content":"In the W20 Umbra book, there was a section in the book discussing the Seelie in the Arcadian Gateway, and how it was super easy to find yourself fighting a duel because there are so many laws and codes of protocol, many of them strange. What are some good strange rules I can have in a Nobles manor that could be interesting plot hooks, especially for crossover games where the outsiders wouldn\u2019t be expecting them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T14:00:32-07:00","id":1450499,"title":"","content":"The Fae of the Arcadia Gateway are reflections of the Fae of the early 1300s. Read up on real duels and social etiquette from the high middle ages or skim some Mallory. That should meet your needs. Failing that, read social histories of ancient Ireland and weird that up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T14:06:06-07:00","id":1450500,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d also suggest looking into folklore, fairy tales, and mythologies and finding all the bizarre rules, taboos, and geases you can spot and using those for inspiration.<br /> <br /> You might have everything from the changelings aren\u2019t allowed to acknowledge anyone whose walking around naked or they might fly off the handle at someone wearing a red shirt on days where the old laws explicitly require blue or they might insist that the fighting be done under the supervision of a specific bear but because they\u2019re hibernating right now you can go but they\u2019ll expect you to come back in spring.<br /> <br /> Dream/Child logic is in full effect the farther into the Dreaming you are so feel free to get wacky, as long as you always remain consistent and obey the letter of the law that you establish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:50:52-07:00","id":1450573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1450476-arcane-laws-of-the-fae?p=1450500#post1450500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d also suggest looking into folklore, fairy tales, and mythologies and finding all the bizarre rules, taboos, and geases you can spot and using those for inspiration.<br /> <br /> You might have everything from the changelings aren\u2019t allowed to acknowledge anyone whose walking around naked or they might fly off the handle at someone wearing a red shirt on days where the old laws explicitly require blue or they might insist that the fighting be done under the supervision of a specific bear but because they\u2019re hibernating right now you can go but they\u2019ll expect you to come back in spring.<br /> <br /> Dream/Child logic is in full effect the farther into the Dreaming you are so feel free to get wacky, as long as you always remain consistent and obey the letter of the law that you establish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcadian Gateway is not in the Dreaming. It's in the Umbra. It's the Umbra's memory of Arcadia, because there used to be Trods from Arcadia to the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1450476-arcane-laws-of-the-fae?p=1450499#post1450499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fae of the Arcadia Gateway are reflections of the Fae of the early 1300s. Read up on real duels and social etiquette from the high middle ages or skim some Mallory. That should meet your needs. Failing that, read social histories of ancient Ireland and weird that up a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need to weird it up. Just take them literally.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also look at the section on navigating Court in Nobles the Shining Host.<br /> Sovereign, the Art, hasn't conceptually changed.<br /> Also. Book of Lost Dreams has a section specifically devoted to this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13114-cuannan","name":"CuAnnan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T23:19:01-07:00","id":1451526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CuAnnan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1450476-arcane-laws-of-the-fae?p=1450573#post1450573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadian Gateway is not in the Dreaming. It's in the Umbra. It's the Umbra's memory of Arcadia, because there used to be Trods from Arcadia to the Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>Although that is the &quot;official version&quot; since Revised when White Wolf rejected almost all crossover elements that existed previously, there is a lot of evidence that the Arcadia Gateway is actually one of the domains of the Far Dreaming and all of its inhabitants actually are fae. If you read the descriptions of the Deepward Road, the Milderwood, and other places in the Changeling sourcebook Dreams &amp; Nightmares, it is <i>clearly</i> describing the Arcadia Gateway (it even name drops Marianna). That book was essential to me when I started designing the Arcadia Gateway in my own Werewolf chronicles and wanted more details of it.<br /> <br /> We're getting into the same territory here as the saying, &quot;The Iliad and Odyssey were not written by Homer, but by a different man by the same name.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Revised era &quot;official version&quot; that purged many crossover elements was done to eliminate turf fights between different developers who each wanted things their own way, and didn't want some other game line to produce canon that would tie their own hands or oblige them to provide the official crossover rules the fans constantly demanded. If you choose to abide by that in your own chronicles, that's fine, but it's no reason to say others are wrong if they prefer the earlier versions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}